{"title":"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2025)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2025)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4adb28e3f5c2257cfd5bd4ab5ee3ea48d1ec889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{4444}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> is written in decimal notation, the sum of its digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Find the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are written in decimal notation.)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6edcbee42ba453beea44fd31723dc36f6a4432.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4444^{4444}&lt;10000^{4444}=\\left(10^4\\right)^{4444}=10^{17776}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4adb28e3f5c2257cfd5bd4ab5ee3ea48d1ec889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{4444}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> has fewer than 17776 digits. This shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1153d0e3578cc835ae077838a28a9dd9b655ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&lt;9\\cdot 17776=159984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"15\" />. The sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is then maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211c23a3239250406ead381dd173ddcb64ba2760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=99999$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/7077addf5008848ab2db41d3dea146eb0e7f4d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\leq 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />. Note that out of all of the positive integers less than or equal to 45, the maximal sum of the digits is 12.\n</p><p>It's not hard to prove that any base-10 number is congruent to the sum of its digits modulo 9. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db8d9eb408614334537b8f4cbd7d6cbc6601cf7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{4444}\\equiv A\\equiv B(\\bmod{9})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"19\" />. This motivates us to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b682582cc23d4bb201af56455ed7b6d86f68575d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq X \\leq 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/added2975a0286cb6bb30972d705023a89ad2967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{4444}\\equiv X(\\bmod{9})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />. The easiest way to do this is by searching for a pattern. Note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65c0803e20299249c2bcd4f2182d5a73b7f8e342.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4444^1\\equiv 7(\\bmod 9), \\ \\ 4444^2\\equiv 4(\\bmod 9), \\ \\ 4444^3\\equiv 1(\\bmod 9)\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a6ad219deed9e985ad3fc9c1db515e8ed07c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444=3\\times 1481+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"158\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66bfe76877afb4d0fcd53de210b267913af1c9c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4444^{4444}\\equiv 4444^{3\\times1481+1}\\equiv \\left(4444^3\\right)^{1481}\\times 4444\\equiv 1\\times 4444\\equiv 7(\\bmod 9)\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff7d0479a20c6e54fdd8d0d6d37a994920f82b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=7$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, which means that the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/94152541528ed008abea53ff30e18a07a3c37f51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~minor edits by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Kevinchen_yay\">KevinChen_Yay</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In what follows, all numbers are assumed to be written in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nGiven a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/37986d8718d30ac080dc149993ba58ed882a183d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> denote the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />,\nand let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d69e362f366c741fd16c826bf946829f5e0e0ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let us start with the following lemma (everybody seems to take it\nas known, but a short proof is in order):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9cfb3fa2fc4d8d50633948acc4817b84c3b0bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{Lemma:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348a60b6d73d27d747678e91f35f99e119b24337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\equiv S(N)\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e3382a8daef9207f6fa8ba6cde5730908f967588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{Proof:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />  To get the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a986cc14441cddb42d759b267ff27c1c799552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, \\dots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />,\nwe successively make integer division by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and the quotients\nof the previous integer division.  Specifically,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1db3c740f9d7d86da3439b5f811e8154a9c18aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = n_0 = 10 n_1 + a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/71538ccacb0d65f0a0bf79c67bd8afc3045974f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 = 10 n_2 + a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f839e6629ef743b23059e15456e190508df92f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2 = 10 n_3 + a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c5610c5030fa7e627f9a5caabb5710e6bcccdf9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.\\ .\\ .\\ .\\ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"4\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9cd95b996b0c895f91471ddee37d7314c7cba05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_k = 10 n_{k+1} + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c5610c5030fa7e627f9a5caabb5710e6bcccdf9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.\\ .\\ .\\ .\\ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"4\" />\n</p><p>(The process is clearly finite since there are finitely many digits.\nAt some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b7b3dd2960f98387792d451ec37b7c15cac296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and we stop.)\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2e3a91c9f93039f8e529f9f1ff9ecc240a028f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(N) = \\sum_{k \\ge 0} a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"115\" height=\"45\" />.  Adding, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/6864d57ebe4d5992ee4f0173d512631c40b184de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + \\sum_{k \\ge 1} n_k = 10 \\sum_{k \\ge 1} n_k + S(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"247\" height=\"45\" />,\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b1aa2e36688c2a8ea2e47d5a4ecaf26d1a24d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 9 \\sum_{k \\ge 1} n_k + S(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"168\" height=\"45\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348a60b6d73d27d747678e91f35f99e119b24337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\equiv S(N)\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This proves the lemma.\n</p><p>To give an answer to the question in the problem, denote\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f7164c4855e3ef5a23e634e7477680fac8f59718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k = 4444^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cbb2691f489deb2c005c5d705a7c94191a4d456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444 \\equiv 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> (since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c36fac91508855adc15465918a29f50f78ef6a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444 = 9*493 + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />).  Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f20a1ce805793421d0e4a9f961cb6ceeec28cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^k \\equiv 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"22\" />\nwhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0145da07837b85dd813b41eabae21532546aea0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,\nplus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77eb11b4857b26333a2e4c4533e171264182bd20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^k \\equiv 4\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"22\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93818b906f3701b16629b3b934fac91bbc391dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/771547fab428047436027d957e1942db4dfccfd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^k \\equiv 1\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"22\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6a119aa2eddda4ebfaeccfbc9430670e296cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We can see this easily by induction.  The case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is clear.\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0145da07837b85dd813b41eabae21532546aea0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab224a1d83b07b14abaab26690e70f632dd26648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{k+1} = 4444^k \\cdot 4444 \\equiv 7 \\cdot 7 = 49 \\equiv 4\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"384\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14247c39d8c119f6a6b2a297220dc6b041148d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{k+2} = 4444^{k+1} \\cdot 4444 \\equiv 4 \\cdot 7 = 28 \\equiv 1\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>And finally,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c2486f267c3fc505ae900277c19c0b1aaf5ab3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{k+3} = 4444^{k+2} \\cdot 4444 \\equiv 1 \\cdot 7 = 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"358\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>In the notation of the problem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9bd083101178e0abc71e7c8d7f86d68bbc3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2728307e40bb31dfe2e5fb9f68d818155873f246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = S(N_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dffee9f79f7f7eb45b3218995daa6b5d8101bcaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = S(A) = S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />, and we want to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc8203bbc2cb4c20867ca8b4080d03967a2abf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(B) = S(S(S(N_k)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We clearly have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3c8d0e7b50889761d20fa6165c6b7fe20cc8dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k \\equiv S(N_k) \\equiv S(S(N_k)) \\equiv \\dots \\equiv S(S(\\dots(S(N_k)\\dots)) \\equiv 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"532\" height=\"20\" />,\nif we apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> enough number of times, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8589071747a266b61ea6693f1906bbfe93b93ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple\nof <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The essence of the problem is to prove that if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9bd083101178e0abc71e7c8d7f86d68bbc3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> then it is enough to apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times to get the result\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  In other words, we want to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01aa1bc52223735656ec55984294b78962aee205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(S(S(S(N_k)))) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />\n(i.e. the number of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/21796ea0b8b3e0f974249141f9e4f81a413b5d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(N_k)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />).\n</p><p>First, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74252c4446a96c976313ce11831e070c49970ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(4444^{k+1}) \\le L(4444^k) + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"22\" />.  This is clear,\nif we think of how we multiply a number (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/0034537f14d15dfca8ac3d21aedc410c2a4655a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> in our case) by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8589071747a266b61ea6693f1906bbfe93b93ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, like we learned to do in 1st or 2nd grade.  It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34d5d5e1ec1d3580467abad3bfa9280b339a27a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(4444^k) \\le 4 k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"22\" />.  Then, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5dbdaecd0cdcec69e751eec6820f581d5e262b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(N_k) \\le 4k \\cdot 9 = 36 k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9bd083101178e0abc71e7c8d7f86d68bbc3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d950bc72b30d81396ea81beebac4705f00a9b3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(N_k) \\le 36 \\cdot 4444 = 159984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />.  We want to\nobtain a bound on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215ffbb0ca9cd44d9f02f317acd9d84b3fe6f07d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9bd083101178e0abc71e7c8d7f86d68bbc3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.  We want the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />,\nsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff9e11571bd45ccf7b4e1b20b81f21335d668118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\le 159984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> has the largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d001c1573fca40efa0666bf32969960bcf9916c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(M)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" />.\nClearly this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3a5b0a47361322d22fbe7f9dc1b6804f5f5cb32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = 99999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c92f721bdbb6b7df9125015b7d41d582b83a746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\le S(M) = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437d16503f2f809356d3e8cb3b43241fccbf6e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\le 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25cac18dc112c97bcf637c56bb97aca3db9c3dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\equiv 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" /> it follows\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215ffbb0ca9cd44d9f02f317acd9d84b3fe6f07d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> is one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/3709123e0821ce75ce7c4517bd60e5b4abc6b084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7, 16, 25, 34, 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />.  In each of these cases\nthe sum of the digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c50e7bedc71cef625f8a7431b31ca2c95a46890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(N_k))) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d9bd083101178e0abc71e7c8d7f86d68bbc3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This solves the problem.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, November 2025]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_November_2025.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2025)\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2025)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, November 2025)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a13743f0019a51abbaa321af540802715548bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />:  Out of curiosity, let us see what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/21796ea0b8b3e0f974249141f9e4f81a413b5d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(N_k)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> for\nall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49bd9cbf3973e910f9e3b4877ffffc96c6d352ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le 4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />.  The proof above shows that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0145da07837b85dd813b41eabae21532546aea0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93818b906f3701b16629b3b934fac91bbc391dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437d16503f2f809356d3e8cb3b43241fccbf6e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\le 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d19dadedc53020b6a7bf47c63e51e1756fdfaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\equiv 4\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215ffbb0ca9cd44d9f02f317acd9d84b3fe6f07d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> is one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad47c72b67166a6faa769dceb94835f3bfd405cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 13, 22, 31, 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />.  In each case, the sum of the\ndigits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6a119aa2eddda4ebfaeccfbc9430670e296cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), the possible values for\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215ffbb0ca9cd44d9f02f317acd9d84b3fe6f07d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6ed7626e9a59f440e9db42be46df8b6dd6dbfd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 10, 19, 28, 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />.  The sum of the digits could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  So we could only conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80dfeedc44ef2c8347593a214223179fe0f3e654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(S(N_k)))) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, that is,\nwe need to apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f4974d7b088479a8eb32891d86d0b46aedb5c363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{2}$\" width=\"9\" height=\"12\" />:  The argument in Solution 2, can be used to show that we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e071c648d8041cb8adc39123b829d5370c11681d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(N_k)))) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> much larger that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8589071747a266b61ea6693f1906bbfe93b93ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.  For example, take\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c25db607fc5d85d83ddceada31ce6c963991a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 22222222$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />.  We want to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cde609e5011b3a7800d4de35aa102bbbb24bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(4444^{22222222}))) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Repeating the argument above, we see that if we denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd02278e63211107ca053cd5a2559c89b89572e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 4444^{22222222}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed394581391dcb77cc73b2850b2f96959fb827a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(N) \\le 4 \\cdot 22222222$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a652dc6722f144484c7efd3335a2d90a53786d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) \\le 4 \\cdot 22222222 \\cdot 9 = 799999992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"20\" />.\n(In fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b5bef9bf013e125f0dc466ffb37307bc4b8c09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(N) = 81061645$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />; I did not compute this, I had a computer\nprogram do the computation.)  Now, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebe1794414ce27c4413e77420381e3fcd4fd170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\le 799999992$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"17\" />,\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> has the largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d001c1573fca40efa0666bf32969960bcf9916c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(M)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" />.  This is clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f876a0d21a078f0dfc278cd05c9a1239c1f44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = 799999989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />.\nThen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e91c7fd2ebcde67a37b6f2a73640e893df4a646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(M) = 78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a911468cee36b1bef7d3dc34e2486b3f23af959e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N)) \\le S(M) = 78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />.  Since we also have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa20dbe9ef733ace72761eb4345bfffa6a0457c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N)) \\equiv 7\\ (\\bmod\\ 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804bbd9b6a378fbe8b42e8b3cf5e24047e527858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> is one of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7c4bb34dc744fcc3912ed8451a93abe27cb649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7, 16, 25, 34, 43, 52, 61, 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"17\" />.  In each of these cases the sum of\nthe digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cde609e5011b3a7800d4de35aa102bbbb24bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(S(4444^{22222222}))) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Note that this argument fails for the next number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/020dd9247d5bc8be418d1c6793e07b93781fea72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 22222225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />.\nIn this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b29d0f297099993aed2c9bf949f4244bc11d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k)) \\le 36 \\cdot 22222225 = 800000100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />.  The\nnumber <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> in this case would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc42ecd6c5da2d53710b786e0352e72bf820e671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$79999999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a6dfe937a217bc7fc14295c5aea9999ff2471c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(M) = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8b908d15627ea3a118bb38668d865edf722170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is also a possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215ffbb0ca9cd44d9f02f317acd9d84b3fe6f07d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(S(N_k))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, whose digits add\nto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Note that it is the argument which fails.  We could\nobtain a sharper bound on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd69d1117d55e072adb05452943919c86295039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(N_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, for example\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afc37bc3eda8e5103430f5fdbdacbab208a9c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L(N_k) \\le 3 \\cdot 22222225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />, which would allow the argument to\nstill yield some \"good\" numbers.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d349451f157180bef169527de7d4499465377c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />: I don't think it would have been easy in the year 1975,\nbut today, 50 years later, one can write a very simple computer program,\nwhich computes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48a0cdbb4296a9e50b6f6c877fed6412987c584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(B) = S(S(S(4444^{4444})))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"21\" />.  One possibility is a\nprogram which calculates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4adb28e3f5c2257cfd5bd4ab5ee3ea48d1ec889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444^{4444}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, converts it to a string, and\ndoes the necessary string operations, conversions and additions.  A\nnicer and more efficient program is one that uses integer divisions.\nHere is an example of such a program in python (one of the languages\nfashionable today):\n</p>\n<pre>  # Compute the sum of the digits of a number.\n  # Instead of doing a modulo operation followed by an integer\n  # division, we do just one integer division, a multiplication\n  # and a subtraction.\n  def sum_digits(number):\n     total_sum = 0\n     while number &gt; 0:\n        # do integer division by 10\n        quotient = number // 10\n        # get the last digit;\n        # we could have done\n        # digit = number&#160;% 10\n        # but this is more efficient\n        digit = number - 10*quotient\n        total_sum = total_sum + digit\n        number = quotient\n     return total_sum\n  \n  N = 4444**4444\n  \n  # compute S(N) = A\n  S_of_N = sum_digits(N)\n  print(\"the sum of the digits is\", S_of_N)\n  \n  # compute S(S(N)) = B\n  S_of_S_of_N = sum_digits(S_of_N)\n  print(\"the sum of the sum of the digits is\", S_of_S_of_N)\n  \n  # compute S(S(S(N))) = S(B)\n  S_of_S_of_S_of_N = sum_digits(S_of_S_of_N)\n  print(\"the sum of the sum of the sum of the digits is\", S_of_S_of_S_of_N)\n</pre>\n<p>Note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09f91618eb5e362a0875cb58faf0e298fcee879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 4444^{4444}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" /> this programs runs in a fraction\nof a second on a laptop.  By contrast, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd02278e63211107ca053cd5a2559c89b89572e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 4444^{22222222}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />,\nthe program takes many days to complete.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO\" title=\"1975 IMO\">1975 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=849354&amp;sid=dfbd2a1b3c3bf405ed1933757f19bbec#p849354\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016203106\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.073 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 868/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30193/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.294      1 -total\n 51.14%    6.798      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 47.84%    6.360      1 Template:IMO_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10886:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016203106 and revision id 271757. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}